<LegalLayout
  title="Pair Journey Privacy Policy — Victor Odukoya"
  description="Privacy Policy for Pair Journey - Learn Anything with Pairs."
  lastUpdated="November 17, 2026"
>
  <p><strong>Pre-release notice:</strong> Pair Journey is not yet available in the app stores. This page describes the planned launch features and will be updated before release to match the services and settings in the published app.</p>

  <p class="lead">
    This Privacy Policy specifically covers the Pair Journey app. Please also review our
    <a href="/privacy">General Privacy Policy</a> for information that applies to all our
    apps and services.
  </p>

  <h2>1. About Pair Journey</h2>
  <p>
    Pair Journey is a learning app that helps you master any topic through pair-matching games.
    You can create custom catalogs of word pairs, use AI to generate content, and track your
    learning progress.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data We Collect in Pair Journey</h2>

  <h3>2.1 User Content</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Catalogs:</strong> Custom catalogs you create, including names, descriptions, and pairs</li>
    <li><strong>Progress Data:</strong> XP, levels, streaks, achievements, and mastery tracking</li>
    <li><strong>Settings:</strong> App preferences, theme choices, and notification settings</li>
    <li><strong>Groups:</strong> Organizational groups for your catalogs</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.2 Gameplay Data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Session statistics (pairs solved, time, accuracy)</li>
    <li>Game mode preferences</li>
    <li>Difficulty adaptation metrics</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.3 AI Generation Data</h3>
  <p>When you use AI to generate catalogs:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The selected topic, description, language, and any source content needed for the requested action are sent through our server to the configured AI provider.</li>
    <li>OpenAI GPT-6 Luna Fast is the planned provider. The hosted provider configuration and retention settings are not yet confirmed.</li>
    <li>Generated content is returned to the app and stored locally; it is included in cloud backup only if you enable that feature.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Data Storage</h2>

  <h3>3.1 Local Storage (Default)</h3>
  <p>
    Catalogs, progress, settings, and gameplay data are stored locally by default. Using account sign-in, AI generation,
    advertising, purchases, or cloud backup may send the data needed for that feature to the relevant service. Exact
    collection and transfer details must be checked against the release build before this draft is published.
  </p>

  <h3>3.2 Cloud Sync (Pro Feature)</h3>
  <p>If you enable cloud sync:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A backup of your catalogs, pairs, progress, statistics, and settings is uploaded to your private account storage on Supabase. It is not end-to-end encrypted.</li>
    <li>Data is associated with your account. Sign-in methods include Apple and Google where supported by the platform.</li>
    <li>You can restore your data on any device</li>
    <li>Canceling Pro does not itself delete the account or cloud backup. Use the app’s cloud-data deletion or account-deletion controls to request deletion.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Advertisements</h2>
  <p>
    Advertising is planned for the free version through Google AdMob. Depending on the final SDK
    configuration and consent choices, the ad service may process device identifiers, technical
    information, and ad interaction data. Whether personalized ads are enabled has not yet been verified.
  </p>
  <p>Planned options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Manage consent choices where required by the applicable region</li>
    <li>Upgrade to Pro to remove all advertisements</li>
    <li>Manage ad preferences through your device settings</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The exact consent flow, regional settings, and SDK behavior must be verified against the release build before this policy is finalized.</p>

  <h2>5. In-App Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Pair Journey Pro subscriptions are processed through the App Store (iOS) or Google Play
    (Android). We use RevenueCat to manage subscriptions.
  </p>
  <p>We receive:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Subscription status and product purchased</li>
    <li>Pseudonymous subscriber identifiers</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Payment details are processed by Apple or Google; Pair Journey does not receive the user’s full payment-card number.</p>

  <h2>6. Notifications</h2>
  <p>Pair Journey may send local notifications for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Daily streak reminders (if enabled)</li>
    <li>Learning goal reminders (if configured)</li>
    <li>Achievement celebrations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can manage notification settings within the app or through your device settings.
    Notifications are generated locally and do not require internet.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Offline Functionality</h2>
  <p>
    Learning from catalogs stored on your device works offline. AI generation, sign-in, purchases, advertising, and cloud
    backup or sync use an internet connection.
  </p>
  <p>Features requiring internet:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>AI-powered catalog generation</li>
    <li>Advertising and purchase verification</li>
    <li>Cloud backup and sync</li>
    <li>Account sign-in/sign-out</li>
    <li>Subscription verification</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Data Export and Deletion</h2>

  <h3>8.1 Export Your Data</h3>
  <p>
    You can export all your Pair Journey data (catalogs, progress, settings) from the app
    settings. Data is exported in JSON format.
  </p>

  <h3 id="data-deletion">8.2 Delete Your Data</h3>
  <p>To delete your Pair Journey data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local data:</strong> Uninstall the app or use "Clear Data" in settings</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud account and data:</strong> Use Settings → Account → Delete Account in Pair Journey, or <a href="/delete-account">request deletion on the web</a> if you no longer have access to the app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Deleting your account does not cancel an App Store or Google Play subscription; cancel it separately through the store where you subscribed. Provider-side backup and log retention periods must be confirmed before release and added here.</p>

  <h2>9. Retention</h2>
  <p>Local data remains on your device until you remove it or uninstall the app, subject to operating-system backup behavior. Cloud backup can be removed using the app’s deletion controls or account deletion. Provider-side processing logs, backups, and legally required records may have separate retention periods; these periods remain to be confirmed before release.</p>

  <h2>10. Age Restrictions</h2>
  <p>
    Pair Journey is intended for adults aged 18 and over for its initial release. The app will not ask users to confirm
    their age in an in-app self-declaration dialog. Store age ratings and access settings have not yet been finalized.
    This intended audience is not an age verification measure.
  </p>

